This project contains a modified subset of FlashAttention-2, derived from
vllm-project/flash-attention commit 28e862d21806bc3580207aa0ad4e2759151e9827,
itself a fork of Dao-AILab/flash-attention.

The plugin's patch is cut against that revision; fa2/PIN records the revision
that vLLM pins and that the sources are checked against. fa2-fp8kv.patch records
the CUDA source diff; check_upstream.py verifies that applying it reproduces all
mapped project sources byte-for-byte. See README.md for the file mapping.

FlashAttention headers retain their original copyright notices and BSD
3-Clause license. See licenses/flash-attention-BSD-3-Clause.txt and
licenses/flash-attention-AUTHORS.

The CUDA adapter and vLLM integration are Apache-2.0 licensed.
The adapter for vLLM 0.27.1 derives from that version's FlashInfer backend and
retains its upstream notices. It includes earlier speculative-decoding
integration work; the FA2 path bypasses FlashInfer attention planning.

The vLLM 0.29 plugin uses the FlashAttention backend interface, metadata
builder and KV-write operation from vLLM, licensed Apache-2.0. It registers
through vLLM's backend plugin API and leaves the stock source files intact.

Local modifications add paged FP8 E4M3 KV loading, BF16 conversion,
split-KV decoding, GQA row packing with causal remapping, asynchronous
FP8 staging, and CUDA Graph compatible vLLM metadata handling.

CUTLASS and FlashInfer are external build dependencies with their own
licenses. They are not relicensed by this repository.

The bounded prefill unpacking approach was informed by 1Cat-vLLM's public
long-context prefill reports, including 1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM PR #212. This
implementation uses a local SM86 gather operation and vLLM's native FA2.
